## Scope

Generate option structs (`ExtractOptions`, `SearchOptions`, `HashOptions`) via Tera templates with proper Go field names matching CLI flags.

## Why this matters

Option structs are the Go-idiomatic alternative to boolean flag parameters. They must map correctly from CLI flag names (kebab-case) to Go field names (PascalCase).

## Implementation guidance

1. Extend the Tera template to generate option structs:

```go
// ExtractOptions configures PDF extraction behavior
type ExtractOptions struct {
    // OCRLanguage sets the OCR language (default: "en")
    OCRLanguage string

    // FirstPage specifies the first page to extract (1-indexed, 0 = all)
    FirstPage int

    // LastPage specifies the last page to extract (0 = to end)
    LastPage int

    // DPI sets the resolution for rasterization
    DPI int

    // OCRMode enables/disables OCR
    OCRMode string

    // ImageFormat controls output image format
    ImageFormat string
}

// SearchOptions configures text search behavior
type SearchOptions struct {
    // CaseSensitive enables case-sensitive search
    CaseSensitive bool

    // WholeWord matches whole words only
    WholeWord bool

    // Regex treats query as regular expression
    Regex bool

    // MaxResults limits the number of results returned
    MaxResults int
}

// HashOptions configures document fingerprinting
type HashOptions struct {
    // Algorithm sets the hash algorithm (e.g., "sha256", "md5")
    Algorithm string

    // Granularity sets hash granularity (page, document, region)
    Granularity string
}
```

2. Add a mapping comment or doc that shows CLI flag → Go field:
- `--ocr-language` → `OCRLanguage`
- `--first-page` → `FirstPage`
- `--last-page` → `LastPage`
- `--dpi` → `DPI`
- `--ocr-mode` → `OCRMode`
- `--image-format` → `ImageFormat`
- `--case-sensitive` → `CaseSensitive`
- `--whole-word` → `WholeWord`
- `--regex` → `Regex`
- `--max-results` → `MaxResults`

## Acceptance criteria

- Option structs are generated in `methods.go` via Tera template
- All 3 option structs exist: `ExtractOptions`, `SearchOptions`, `HashOptions`
- All struct fields are exported (PascalCase)
- CLI flag mapping is documented in comments
- Generated code compiles with `go build ./pdftract-go`

