## Scope

Implement the 9 contract methods as stubs that call through to the subprocess engine, establishing the execution path from SDK to binary.

## Why this matters

This completes the SDK public API by wiring the method signatures to the actual execution engine. The methods will initially be stub implementations that validate the contract and subprocess integration.

## Implementation guidance

For each of the 9 methods, implement a stub that:

1. Validates inputs (non-nil context, valid source)
2. Constructs the appropriate subprocess command
3. Executes via the subprocess engine (use the existing subprocess.go)
4. Parses output into the appropriate return type
5. Returns errors via the error handling system (bf-30n82s)

Example pattern for `Extract`:
```go
func (c *Client) Extract(ctx context.Context, source Source, opts *ExtractOptions) (*Document, error) {
    if opts == nil {
        opts = &ExtractOptions{}
    }

    // Build subprocess command
    cmd := []string{"extract"}
    if opts.OCRLanguage != "" {
        cmd = append(cmd, "--ocr-language", opts.OCRLanguage)
    }
    // ... add other options

    // Execute via subprocess engine
    output, err := c.exec(ctx, source, cmd)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }

    // Parse output into Document
    var doc Document
    if err := json.Unmarshal(output, &doc); err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("failed to parse document: %w", err)
    }

    return &doc, nil
}
```

For streaming methods (`ExtractStream`, `Search`):
- Create a buffered channel (size 16)
- Spawn goroutine to read subprocess output
- Send `PageResult` or `MatchResult` structs to channel
- Return receive-only channel (`<-chan`)

## Acceptance criteria

- All 9 methods exist in `methods.go` with implementations
- Each method validates inputs and returns errors via error system
- Streaming methods return `<-chan` types with buffered channels
- `go build ./pdftract-go` succeeds
- Methods are documented with godoc comments
- Integration with subprocess engine is demonstrated (even if stubs)

## References

- Plan: SDK Architecture / The Ten SDKs, line 3474
- Depends on: Child 1 (types must exist), Child 2 (methods generated), Child 3 (option structs)

## Scope

Define all core data types in `pdftract-go/types.go` that will be used as return types for the SDK contract methods.

## Why this matters

These types are the foundational data structures for the entire SDK. All contract methods return instances of these types, so they must be defined before methods can be generated.

## Implementation guidance

Create `pdftract-go/types.go` with the following exported struct types:

```go
package pdftract

// Document represents a complete PDF document extraction result
type Document struct {
    Pages []Page
    Metadata *Metadata
    // Add other fields as needed per plan
}

// Page represents a single page in the document
type Page struct {
    PageNumber int
    Content string
    // Add other fields as needed
}

// Metadata represents PDF document metadata
type Metadata struct {
    Title string
    Author string
    Subject string
    Keywords string
    Creator string
    Producer string
    CreationDate string
    ModDate string
    PageCount int
    // Add other fields as needed
}

// Fingerprint represents a document hash for change detection
type Fingerprint struct {
    Hash string
    Algorithm string
    // Add other fields as needed
}

// Classification represents document classification results
type Classification struct {
    Category string
    Confidence float64
    // Add other fields as needed
}

// PageResult represents a streamed page extraction result
type PageResult struct {
    PageNumber int
    Content string
    Error error
}

// MatchResult represents a search match result
type MatchResult struct {
    PageNumber int
    Match string
    Context string
    Error error
}

// Receipt represents extraction metadata for verification
type Receipt struct {
    // Define per plan requirements
}
```

All types MUST be exported (PascalCase) and have exported fields.

## Acceptance criteria

- `pdftract-go/types.go` exists with all 7 types defined
- All types are exported (PascalCase names)
- All struct fields are exported (PascalCase)
- `go build ./pdftract-go` succeeds
- Types match the plan's contract method return types

