## Scope

Implement detect_conformance(metadata_stream: Option<&[u8]>) -> Option<String>. Parse the catalog's /Metadata stream as XMP XML using quick-xml; extract pdfaid:part and pdfaid:conformance namespace elements; combine as \"PDF/A-{part}{conformance}\" (e.g. \"PDF/A-1b\", \"PDF/A-2u\").

Also: move quick-xml from the ocr feature gate to the default feature set (per plan note line 1120) since conformance detection is a default-on capability.

## Why this matters

PDF/A conformance is the archival-grade contract: PDF/A-1b, PDF/A-2u, PDF/A-3a, etc. each have different downstream consumer requirements (long-term archival, accessibility, embedded files allowed). Knowing the conformance level lets RAG pipelines, archival systems, and compliance tools route the document correctly. Without it, downstream code must guess from the producer string or assume worst-case.

## Implementation guidance

- Public API: detect_conformance(metadata_stream: Option<&[u8]>) -> Option<String>
- Crate: quick-xml = \"0.36\" (move from ocr feature to default)
- Implementation:
  ```rust
  use quick_xml::events::Event;
  use quick_xml::reader::Reader;

  pub fn detect_conformance(metadata_stream: Option<&[u8]>) -> Option<String> {
      let xml = metadata_stream?;
      let mut reader = Reader::from_reader(xml);
      let mut part: Option<String> = None;
      let mut conf: Option<String> = None;
      let mut current_tag: Option<Vec<u8>> = None;
      let mut buf = Vec::new();
      loop {
          match reader.read_event_into(&mut buf) {
              Ok(Event::Start(e)) => {
                  let name = e.name().as_ref().to_vec();
                  if name.ends_with(b\"pdfaid:part\") || name.ends_with(b\":part\") { /* track */ }
                  if name.ends_with(b\"pdfaid:conformance\") || name.ends_with(b\":conformance\") { /* track */ }
                  current_tag = Some(name);
              }
              Ok(Event::Text(e)) => {
                  if let Some(tag) = &current_tag {
                      let text = e.unescape().unwrap_or_default().to_string();
                      if tag.ends_with(b\"pdfaid:part\") || tag.ends_with(b\":part\") { part = Some(text); }
                      if tag.ends_with(b\"pdfaid:conformance\") || tag.ends_with(b\":conformance\") { conf = Some(text); }
                  }
              }
              Ok(Event::End(_)) => current_tag = None,
              Ok(Event::Eof) => break,
              Err(_) => return None,
              _ => {}
          }
          buf.clear();
      }
      match (part, conf) {
          (Some(p), Some(c)) => Some(format!(\"PDF/A-{p}{c}\")),
          (Some(p), None) => Some(format!(\"PDF/A-{p}\")),
          _ => None,
      }
  }
  ```
- Move quick-xml from optional/ocr-gated to default = true in Cargo.toml
- XMP namespace: http://www.aiim.org/pdfa/ns/id/; the prefix is conventionally pdfaid but may be any prefix

## Critical considerations

- XMP uses XML namespaces; the prefix can be anything (pdfaid, x, foo). Match on local name (the part after the colon)
- pdfaid:part is a digit (1, 2, 3, 4); pdfaid:conformance is a letter (a, b, u)
- The combined string format is documented in PDF/A spec: PDF/A-1b, PDF/A-2a, PDF/A-2u, PDF/A-3a, PDF/A-4f
- Malformed XML in /Metadata stream → return None (no error propagation; the catalog might still be parseable)
- Missing /Metadata stream → None (not an error)
- quick-xml is moved to default feature; Cargo.toml diff must be reviewed; binary-size impact ~30 KB

## Acceptance criteria

- PDF with XMP /Metadata containing pdfaid:part=1, pdfaid:conformance=b → \"PDF/A-1b\"
- PDF with pdfaid:part=2, pdfaid:conformance=u → \"PDF/A-2u\"
- PDF with only pdfaid:part=3 (no conformance) → \"PDF/A-3\"
- PDF with no XMP metadata → None
- PDF with malformed XMP → None (graceful failure)
- quick-xml is in default feature; cargo tree shows it without --features ocr
- Critical test PDFs from PDF/A test corpus pass

