## Scope

Implement the /Catalog /Names /EmbeddedFiles name tree walker. Name trees (PDF 1.7 7.9.6) are number-tree-like structures keyed by PdfString instead of integer. Walks the tree and returns Vec<(filespec_name, FilespecRef)>.

Module: crates/pdftract-core/src/attachment/embedded_files.rs.

## Why this matters

The /EmbeddedFiles name tree is the legacy location for embedded attachments in PDF 1.x (still used by PDF portfolios). Without this walker, embedded files in legacy PDFs are invisible to extraction.

## Implementation guidance

- Locate /Catalog /Names /EmbeddedFiles via document catalog (absent → empty Vec)
- Name tree structure (recursive):
  - /Kids: array of child node refs (internal nodes)
  - /Names: array alternating [key, value, key, value, ...] (leaf nodes)
  - /Limits: array [low, high] for range-based traversal optimization
- Walker:
  ```rust
  pub fn walk_name_tree(resolver: &XrefResolver, root: ObjRef) -> Vec<(String, ObjRef)> {
      let mut out = Vec::new();
      walk_recursive(resolver, root, &mut out);
      out
  }
  fn walk_recursive(resolver, node_ref, out) {
      let node = resolver.resolve(node_ref);
      if let Some(kids) = node.get(\"Kids\") {
          for kid_ref in kids.as_array() { walk_recursive(resolver, *kid_ref, out); }
      } else if let Some(names) = node.get(\"Names\") {
          for chunk in names.chunks(2) {
              let key = chunk[0].as_string().to_string();
              let value = chunk[1].as_ref();
              out.push((key, value));
          }
      }
  }
  ```
- Keys are PdfStrings (UTF-16BE BOM-prefixed or PDFDocEncoded); decode via Phase 1 PdfString decoder
- Values are indirect refs to /Filespec dicts

## Critical considerations

- Name trees may have arbitrary depth; Box recursion or iterative stack to avoid stack overflow on pathological trees
- /Limits is an optimization hint; ignore for correctness, use for fast range lookup if needed
- Filespec resolution is sibling 7.5.2's responsibility; this bead returns the refs only

## Acceptance criteria

- PDF with /EmbeddedFiles tree containing 5 attachments → returns 5 (String, ObjRef) pairs
- PDF with no /EmbeddedFiles → empty Vec
- Deep nested tree (5 levels) → walks correctly
- Keys decode correctly from UTF-16BE strings

